From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:27:32 -0800
Subject: [Media] Re-enable kDisallowMixedOpaqueMediaResponses by default

Re-enable kDisallowMixedOpaqueMediaResponses by default on trunk now
that UrlData::CanAcceptDataFrom() CHECK crashes (crbug.com/579225207)
and MultiBuffer cross-origin redirect handling (crbug.com/573441094) are
fixed (also enabling post-redirect Service Worker skipping gated on the
same killswitch). Restore the web-test expectations that were
temporarily suppressed in crrev.com/c/8677461.

Bug: 572307225, 572363265, 573441094, 579225207
Change-Id: I87bef363a1dd1882b8ec77bfb08242d5445a5692
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8685646
Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1734709}

diff --git a/media/base/media_switches.cc b/media/base/media_switches.cc
index 4442b4a25b98f3e17f9fcec9c8c1997d1d2300fd..e65cdab5c16946833296f299370c0d0249db2655 100644
--- a/media/base/media_switches.cc
+++ b/media/base/media_switches.cc
@@ -523,11 +523,14 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kDeferAudioFocusUntilAudible,
 // (instead of the FFmpegAudioDecoder).
 BASE_FEATURE(kDirectOpusAudioDecoding, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
-// Killswitch for disallowing mixing opaque and non-opaque responses in
+// Killswitch for disallowing mixing opaque and non-opaque responses and
+// skipping Service Workers after network redirects in
 // ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider (crbug.com/572363265).
-// TODO(crbug.com/572363265): Remove after M158 reaches stable.
+// TODO(crbug.com/572363265): Remove killswitch (keeping mixed-opacity responses
+// disallowed and post-redirect Service Worker skipping enabled) after M159
+// reaches stable.
 BASE_FEATURE(kDisallowMixedOpaqueMediaResponses,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 // Adds an animation to document picture-in-picture resizes.
 BASE_FEATURE(kDocumentPictureInPictureAnimateResize,
